The comprehensive safeguards agreement requires a State to establish
and maintain a system of accounting for, and control of, all nuclear material
subject to safeguards, including:
(1)
A measurement system;
(2)
A system for the evaluation of accuracy;
(3)
Procedures for reviewing measurement differences;
(4)
Procedures for carrying out physical inventories;
(5)
A system for the evaluation of unmeasured inventories;
(6)
A records and reports system for all material balance areas;
(7)
A system of reporting to the IAEA.

